# ThesisArena environment.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in your own values. .env.local is gitignored and
# must never be committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nansen (required)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every on-chain read goes through this key. Get one at https://nansen.ai.
# Credits are consumed per call and costs vary by endpoint, so keep it private.
NANSEN_API_KEY=nsn_your_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset  -> local SQLite at data/thesisarena.db, created on first run.
#           No setup needed; this is the default for development.
# Set    -> Postgres. Required for any hosted deployment, because a serverless
#           filesystem is ephemeral and SQLite would vanish between requests.
#
# Use the POOLED connection string. On Neon the host contains "-pooler";
# a direct endpoint exhausts connections under serverless traffic.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-example-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin used when building share-card links. Defaults to localhost.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.example

# Overrides the local SQLite path. Rarely needed.
# THESISARENA_DB=data/thesisarena.db

# Base URL the seeding and scheduler scripts call. Defaults to localhost:3001.
# THESISARENA_URL=http://localhost:3001
